title: What Are We Fighting For?
subtitle: The Senate must set the Republic's war aims.
tags: event
view-if: war and war_begins_seen and war_aim = "" and not finale and not game_ending
max-visits: 1
priority: 4
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_war.svg
on-arrival: {! Q.wc_command = SW.warCommand(Q); !}

= What Are We Fighting For?

The war has begun, and the Senate must decide what it is for. The answer will shape every season of fighting: where the fleets go, whether anyone talks to the enemy, and which of the Caucus's factions can stomach it.

[? if wc_command : The Caucus [? if rc_chancellor : holds the Chancellery?][? if not rc_chancellor : chairs the Security & Defence Committee?], so our view will carry. ?][? if not wc_command and chancellor_bloc != "rim" : The Chancellor's allies want **total victory**. If we propose something else, the Senate will vote on it. ?][? if not wc_command and chancellor_bloc = "rim" : The Chancellor's allies want **the liberation of the Rim**. If we propose something else, the Senate will vote on it. ?]

- @victory: Total victory: the Confederacy must surrender.
- @peace: A negotiated peace, as soon as one can be had.
- @rim: The liberation of the Rim: win back the worlds that left, and fix why they left.

@victory
subtitle: The war goes a little faster; fear runs higher and the peace talks wither. The Hawks are pleased, the Pacifists are not.
on-arrival: {! Q.wc_command = SW.warCommand(Q); SW.setWarAim(Q, 'victory'); !}
go-to: aims_result

@peace
subtitle: The war goes slower; the talks grow. The Pacifists are pleased, the Hawks are not.
on-arrival: {! Q.wc_command = SW.warCommand(Q); SW.setWarAim(Q, 'peace'); !}
go-to: aims_result

@rim
subtitle: The Outer Rim front gets priority, and Rim reforms win seceded worlds back. The Rimward wing is pleased.
on-arrival: {! Q.wc_command = SW.warCommand(Q); SW.setWarAim(Q, 'rim'); !}
go-to: aims_result

@aims_result

[+ vote_html +]

[? if wa_overruled : The Senate rejects our proposal. The Republic will fight for **[+ war_aim_text +]**. ?][? if not wa_overruled : The Republic will fight for **[+ war_aim_text +]**. ?]

*The war aim is shown on the Forces tab. Every second turn, the War Council decides where the Republic commits its strength.*
